{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "market-multivariate-anomalies",
  "title": "Unusual Market Sessions",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "546b862d-1168-4eec-adf0-31d55f16339d",
      "question": "Treat January 2 through June 30, 2026 as the historical baseline for the reviewed assets. Score July 1 through August 31, 2026 and return the 10 asset sessions with the most unusual combined one-day return, five-day return, 20-session realized volatility, and trailing-volume behavior. Explain which observed features made each session unusual, and state clearly that anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor causal explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-09-29T20:28:19.193984Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-09-29T20:30:32.909573Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Top‑10 most anomalous reviewed‑asset sessions (July 1 – August 31 2026)**\n*Baseline: January 2 – June 30 2026*\n\n| Rank | Asset (ID) | Session (UTC) | Anomaly score | Cohort percentile | Key observed deviations* |\n|------|------------|---------------|---------------|-------------------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | **asset‑delta** | 2026‑08‑24 | **1.282** | 100.0 | 1‑day return **+2.38 σ**, 5‑day return **‑0.57 σ**, 20‑day vol **+0.56 σ**, volume **+0.30 σ** |\n| 2 | **asset‑kestrel** | 2026‑08‑06 | **1.175** | 99.81 | 1‑day **+1.00 σ**, 5‑day **‑1.93 σ**, 20‑day vol **+1.20 σ**, volume **‑0.35 σ** |\n| 3 | **asset‑galena** | 2026‑08‑31 | **0.931** | 99.61 | 1‑day **‑0.09 σ**, 5‑day **‑2.92 σ**, 20‑day vol **+2.13 σ**, volume **+0.62 σ** |\n| 4 | **asset‑fathom** | 2026‑07‑14 | **0.906** | 99.42 | 1‑day **‑1.23 σ**, 5‑day **+1.13 σ**, 20‑day vol **+0.65 σ**, volume **+1.13 σ** |\n| 5 | **asset‑juniper** | 2026‑08‑20 | **0.861** | 99.22 | 1‑day **+0.55 σ**, 5‑day **‑1.95 σ**, 20‑day vol **+1.46 σ**, volume **‑0.86 σ** |\n| 6 | **asset‑aether** | 2026‑08‑18 | **0.834** | 99.03 | 1‑day **+2.02 σ**, 5‑day **‑0.35 σ**, 20‑day vol **+0.86 σ**, volume **+0.23 σ** |\n| 7 | **asset‑borealis** | 2026‑07‑22 | **0.829** | 98.84 | 1‑day **‑0.75 σ**, 5‑day **+1.76 σ**, 20‑day vol **‑0.87 σ**, volume **‑0.91 σ** |\n| 8 | **asset‑ember** | 2026‑08‑21 | **0.809** | 98.64 | 1‑day **+0.76 σ**, 5‑day **‑1.51 σ**, 20‑day vol **+1.60 σ**, volume **‑2.23 σ** |\n| 9 | **asset‑harbor** | 2026‑08‑28 | **0.800** | 98.45 | 1‑day **+2.17 σ**, 5‑day **‑0.20 σ**, 20‑day vol **+0.79 σ**, volume **+0.95 σ** |\n|10| **asset‑galena** | 2026‑08‑11 | **0.790** | 98.26 | 1‑day **+0.69 σ**, 5‑day **‑1.74 σ**, 20‑day vol **+0.80 σ**, volume **‑0.14 σ** |\n\n\\*Deviations are expressed as **standard‑score (σ) differences from the baseline distribution** for each of the four features used by the anomaly model:\n\n| Feature | What it measures |\n|---------|-------------------|\n| **adjusted_return_1d** | One‑day adjusted‑close return |\n| **adjusted_return_5d** | Five‑day cumulative adjusted‑close return |\n| **realized_volatility_20d** | 20‑session realized volatility |\n| **log_volume_deviation_20d** | Log‑volume over the trailing 20 sessions (relative to baseline) |\n\n### Why each session stands out\n\n| Asset‑Session | Dominant unusual feature(s) |\n|---------------|----------------------------|\n| **asset‑delta 2026‑08‑24** | Very large positive 1‑day return (+2.38 σ) together with modestly elevated volatility and volume. |\n| **asset‑kestrel 2026‑08‑06** | Combination of a strong positive 1‑day move (+1.00 σ) and a sharply negative 5‑day return (‑1.93 σ) while volatility spikes (+1.20 σ). |\n| **asset‑galena 2026‑08‑31** | Extreme 5‑day loss (‑2.92 σ) and the highest volatility surge in the set (+2.13 σ); volume also above baseline. |\n| **asset‑fathom 2026‑07‑14** | Large negative 1‑day return (‑1.23 σ) but a positive 5‑day return (+1.13 σ) and unusually high volume (+1.13 σ). |\n| **asset‑juniper 2026‑08‑20** | Negative 5‑day return (‑1.95 σ) with elevated volatility (+1.46 σ) and below‑average volume (‑0.86 σ). |\n| **asset‑aether 2026‑08‑18** | Very strong positive 1‑day return (+2.02 σ) with modest volatility rise. |\n| **asset‑borealis 2026‑07‑22** | Positive 5‑day return (+1.76 σ) paired with lower‑than‑usual volatility (‑0.87 σ) and volume (‑0.91 σ). |\n| **asset‑ember 2026‑08‑21** | Elevated volatility (+1.60 σ) and a pronounced volume drop (‑2.23 σ) alongside a negative 5‑day return. |\n| **asset‑harbor 2026‑08‑28** | Large positive 1‑day return (+2.17 σ) with higher volume (+0.95 σ). |\n| **asset‑galena 2026‑08‑11** | Negative 5‑day return (‑1.74 σ) with modestly higher volatility. |\n\n### Important limitation\n> **Anomaly scores describe unusual observed feature combinations; they are not forecasts or probabilities.**\n> **Observed deviations are descriptive reason codes and do not establish a cause or adverse event.**\n\nThese statements are taken directly from the model output’s own limitation notes[1]. The scores simply flag sessions whose joint behavior (return, volatility, volume) was rare relative to the January‑June baseline; they do **not** predict future moves nor explain *why* the moves occurred.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market anomaly scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:457bdfcad68a4ccaf2ef23da3785a1259eff636030f75a85a0af8e905d1c4d5a`",
